<div class="wrapper">
  <div class="swiper collection" data-slide-delay="{{section.settings.slide_delay}}">
    <!-- Additional required wrapper -->
    <div class="swiper-wrapper">
      <!-- Slides -->
      {%- comment -%}
        bd 958r.3 — was `limit: products.size`, i.e. no limit: every product in the collection
        was rendered into the HTML up front (Shopify caps collection.products at 50). This is
        the path the homepage's six Collection Slider sections actually take (the section's
        grid branch only runs when a collection has <=6 products), so it produced ~300
        server-rendered product cards on the homepage. product_limit is passed by the caller;
        default: products.size preserves the old behaviour if the snippet is ever rendered
        without it.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign slider_limit = product_limit | default: products.size -%}
      {% for product in products limit: slider_limit %}
        <div class="swiper-slide">
          {% render 'product-grid-item', product: product %}
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="navigator-box">
    <div class="swiper-button-next"></div>
    <div class="swiper-button-prev swiper-button-disabled"></div>
  </div>
</div>